# Backups created by link.sh when it replaces a real file with a symlink.
*.bak

# Derived harness symlinks. link.sh regenerates these from shared/.agents/;
# committing them would encode one machine's set of installed harnesses.
# ubuntu/.claude/ and ubuntu/.codex/ are ignored by contents so the one real
# settings file in each — settings.json, config.toml — can be negated back in;
# everything else there (AGENTS.md, skills/) is a link.sh symlink.
ubuntu/.claude/*
!ubuntu/.claude/settings.json
# hooks/ is real content, not a link.sh symlink: settings.json names each hook
# script by absolute path, so the snapshot is incomplete without them.
!ubuntu/.claude/hooks/
!ubuntu/.claude/hooks/*
ubuntu/.codex/*
!ubuntu/.codex/config.toml
ubuntu/.codex-kiro/
ubuntu/.gemini/
ubuntu/.kiro/

# Never snapshot SSH material. The sync copies an explicit allowlist and never
# reaches here, and scan-secrets.sh would catch a private key in a listed source —
# but neither guard sees a file copied in by hand. Commit signing keys are
# per-machine and regenerated on rebuild; only the public half belongs in the
# repository, and it already lives in ubuntu/.config/git/allowed_signers.
ubuntu/.ssh/

# Pulled in by tooling that runs inside a synced config directory.
node_modules/

# OS noise.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
